  "long_description": "It costs nearly $12,000 for a patient to spend a single night at a hospital. Delivering care at home is often far less expensive and much more convenient for patients.\r\n\r\nBut robust infrastructure to enable this transition from the hospital to the home is missing. Instead, it’s a patchwork of different vendors, tied together by faxes, phone calls and hours of time by nurses. Durable medical equipment (DME) delivery is a part of healthcare that’s forgotten until it goes wrong.\r\n\r\nVerse’s AI-enabled ordering platform solves these problems, ensuring patients and clinicians have a seamless experience every time.\r\n\r\nWe’re a well-funded Series C company backed by General Catalyst, SignalFire, and Sapphire Ventures, and we’re growing fast. If you want to help move healthcare from the hospital to the home, we’d love to meet you.",
